From 78aad41469b25ac65bb088744b2ed8cc4ad8ac97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Pomeroy <allen@pomeroy.us>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:53:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DELETE accepts '*' and '%' in the file name

DELETE looked a wildcard up as a literal name, so DELETE *.*, F*.COM or
*.*;* failed with "name not found in directory". It never matched
wildcards (no earlier commit did); DIR and SET FILE did. Every match in
the one directory is now deleted, with the same version rules as for
one file: no version (or ;0) the highest, ;n that version, ;-n the n-th
lower, ;* every version. The matches are listed first and deleted by
exact version, so the deletes never disturb the list. A file that
cannot be deleted (a reserved file, a non-empty directory) is reported
and the rest still go; a spec that matches nothing fails.
tests/cli_delete_wildcard_check.sh fails 9 of 12 checks before this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WA1cTvnJjW7a9acesLHq2C
